<body>
    <h1>Dynamics 365 CRM Synapse Links</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 local-id=3D"c4b31f510451" id=3D"Dynamics365CRMSynapseLinks-Depl=
oymentConsiderations">Deployment Considerations</h2>
<p local-id=3D"12dcd7485781">Each Synapse Link must be manually configured =
via the Power Apps UI, no Terraform or Powershell options are documented.</=
p>
<ul local-id=3D"b805f86339bd">
<li local-id=3D"955eddadecde">
<p local-id=3D"561ac482d67c">The user creating the synapse link must have S=
ystem Administrator permission on the Dataverse environment.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"a115341dbebe">
<p local-id=3D"ee2a42f497d1">The user creating the synapse link must have O=
wner permission on the target Storage Account. This permission is strictly =
controlled and only granted to BTS Cloud Team or the DNA OPS Team temporari=
ly.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"43d5dd95319a">
<li local-id=3D"981527a055d2">
<p local-id=3D"9cb082ba0793">The process of creating the initial connection=
 configuration leverages the UI users identity and permissions to obtain th=
e Account Key to the Storage Account and then sets permissions for the Mana=
ged Identity associated with the Enterprise Policy linked to the Dataverse =
database so that it can read/write to the Storage Account.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"5025f7265319">
<p local-id=3D"fca2a43a5685">The creation process dynamically names and cre=
ates the Storage Container within the Storage Account, the name of the Stor=
age Container cannot be set or predicted. The name follows the pattern data=
verse-&lt;formatted dataverse name&gt;-&lt;unique id&gt;</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e6593d4905af">
<p local-id=3D"299cc02ff686">Once the link is initially created, any Datave=
rse user with System Administrator can make changes to it (although under t=
he recommended settings for Databricks Lakeflow Connect there are not setti=
ngs that can be modified once initially configured).</p>
</li>
</ul>
